comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T10:37:06.402Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Root cause reproduced and fixed on the branch pin (@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28): readClosureItems copies bootstrap/schema into the reader unconditionally, and read-side SDK calls stopped recreating missing workflow schema files in pm-cli 2026.10.25 (GH-1568), so a tracker whose schema directory is absent now fails the copy with ENOENT and both previews refuse local_read_failed. Classification: production code relying on old CLI read-side backfill. Fix: copy the schema directory only when it exists in the owned bootstrap copy (mirroring the existing explicit settings repair); reads on the new CLI no longer need schema files. Both previously failing tests pass: node --test --test-name-pattern 'source isolation precedes SDK backfill' test/dependency-closure.test.ts and ...'source isolation precedes SDK scaffolding' test/ownership.test.ts."
  "2026-11-03T12:54:42.296Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Gate evidence on the PR branch: both previously failing tests pass (node --test --test-name-pattern 'source isolation precedes SDK backfill' test/dependency-closure.test.ts, node --test --test-name-pattern 'source isolation precedes SDK scaffolding' test/ownership.test.ts); typecheck, the docstring gate and the changelog check pass. The full local suite is impractical on this host: the machine is saturated by parallel fleet test runs (load above 19 for hours), and the suite's live Linear fetch tests stall for tens of minutes each, so the remaining coverage is left to CI. No schema-copy site besides the fixed one exists in the extension."
  "2026-11-06T15:12:00.383Z",codex-sol,"Issue #188 is already fixed on main by fd16802 (#187): readClosureItems now copies schema only when present in the owned bootstrap. Revalidating both original SDK fixtures and a disposable behavioral revert against current main 682bef8; this closure PR will change tracker evidence and the generated changelog only, with no production or test changes."
  "2026-11-06T15:15:25.751Z",codex-sol,"Current-main verification: npm run build and node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern \"source isolation precedes SDK\" test/dependency-closure.test.ts test/ownership.test.ts pass 2/2 with 0 failures and 0 skips, also through pm test --run --only-last --progress. npm run typecheck and npm run docstring pass (8 files, 112 documented declarations). No separate lint script is configured. The repository pin is SDK 2026.11.4 and is unchanged; npm currently reports CLI 2026.11.6. Original delivery #187 merged fd16802 and its Node 22, Node 26, npm and Bun checks all succeeded. Full unchanged gates will run on the closure PR in CI."
  "2026-11-06T15:16:12.987Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof on unchanged main 682bef8 and SDK 2026.11.4: in a disposable non-git copy, replace only the readClosureItems schema pathExists guard with the prior unconditional cp. Run node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap --test-name-pattern \"source isolation precedes SDK\" test/dependency-closure.test.ts test/ownership.test.ts. Node 22.23.4 and 26.13.0 each pass 2/2 fixed, fail 2/2 reverted with LinearClosureRefusal and LinearOwnershipRefusal (local_read_failed), then pass 2/2 after restoration; all runs have zero skips. Independent fresh-case closure runs for absent schema/statuses.json, history, settings.json and schema each pass 1/1 (both writable and immutable sources across SDK/JSON/TOON). A scratch-only catch at the reverted copy records sanitized underlying diagnostic code=ENOENT, syscall=lstat, confirming the absent schema directory is the failing case. The original source-isolation and unsafe-entry assertions remain unchanged. No production or test files are modified by this closure PR."
  "2026-11-06T15:16:16.073Z",codex-sol,"Verification complete for GitHub #188. The inherited tracker was already closed by #204 as delivered in #187; it was reopened only to follow the required claim/start verification workflow. Leaving this item in progress for orchestrator disposition and releasing only the codex-sol claim. This PR changes only this item, its append-only history, and generated CHANGELOG.md if regeneration changes it. Review and final-head CI outcomes will be reported in the PR and handoff; no merges or releases are authorized."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:51.910Z",codex-sol,"Final pre-push health: pinned pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes (exit 0) under a clean temporary HOME with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, matching CI isolation. The default local environment reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew:2026.11.4:2026.11.5:pm-github; existing pm-linear-bzam tracks host-version skew, so no duplicate follow-up or dependency/config change is needed. Legacy provenance remains advisory and its history is preserved. git diff --check and the closure file allowlist pass; the existing history is a byte-identical prefix of the updated stream."
  "2026-11-06T19:13:43.842Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR209 after CodeRabbit round 1. Thread PRRT_kwDOSYpKlc60oVNt flags future closure losing the original release attribution. Tag v2026.11.04 contains this already-delivered item and package version 2026.11.4. Preserve the owner-required in-progress status, pin its release to 2026.11.4, and validate later closure in a disposable real SDK tracker with an unset-release behavioral control. Keep changes scoped to this item, append-only history, and generated changelog."
  "2026-11-06T19:17:50.839Z",codex-sol,"Fixed CodeRabbit thread PRRT_kwDOSYpKlc60oVNt by setting release=2026.11.4, verified against tag v2026.11.04. The live item remains in_progress for orchestrator closure. Added a self-contained linked SDK regression command: pm test pm-linear-hb2g --run --only-last --progress executes two assertions with a real non-git temporary tracker and the pinned pm-changelog generator. Both assertions failed before the pin (a later closure reappeared in release 2026.11.6 and disappeared from 2026.11.4), and both now pass. Behavioral revert in a disposable SDK copy unsets only release: fixed 2 pass/0 fail; reverted 0 pass/2 fail; restored 2 pass/0 fail. The package checkout was unchanged by this proof. Typecheck and the docstring gate pass (8 files, 112 declarations). Prior issue-188 source-read verification and the original 466-test gates remain recorded; final CI must certify the new metadata head."
  "2026-11-06T19:22:58.523Z",codex-sol,"Review disposition correction after full-generator verification: the CodeRabbit request is conditional on a future status change to closed, which this PR does not perform and the owner reserves for the orchestrator. Pinning release=2026.11.4 while status remains in_progress makes the pinned all-release-tags generator remove the already-published pm-linear-hb2g bullet. Removing the experimental pin restores that bullet. Therefore the previous comment calling the pin the final fix is superseded: retain in_progress without a new completion timestamp, preserve the existing historical entry, and apply release=2026.11.4 together with the orchestrator-owned future closure. The late-closure SDK experiment and its two failing controls remain in append-only history; its prospective pinned-state test is unlinked because that is not this PR state. No existing test or threshold was removed or weakened. Respond to PRRT_kwDOSYpKlc60oVNt with these applicability and generated-output receipts."
  "2026-11-06T19:23:03.696Z",codex-sol,Canonical-checkout local health reports two pre-existing clone-local merge receipts. Pinned pm merge reconcile --dry-run refuses merge_receipt_not_portable and writes no audit history; preserve those receipts and existing history rather than stage unrelated evidence or force repair. Prior CI health passed in a clean checkout; the new head must get fresh CI. No new PM CLI/SDK gap is claimed.
